1
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:11,610
Cinderella's Sister

2
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:21,200
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,300
Episode 3

4
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,100
Why did you hit her?

5
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:43,000
Something like that shouldn't happen.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,600
I did it because she is so cold toward Hyo Seon.

7
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:52,000
I see Hyo Seon annoying Eun Jo too much.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,600
She is naturally a block of ice.

9
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:00,400
When she did it right in front of me, I was so angry I also did it without realizing.

10
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:05,500
Saying you are angry, did you raise her by beating her up every time you were angry?

11
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,200
You will be scolded for doing something shameful.

12
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,400
Don't do that again.

13
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:13,100
It drew your attention.

14
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,800
I was afraid you would hate my daughter for being mean to yours.

15
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:21,000
I didn't know what you would do if you noticed it.

16
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:27,600
Who noticed such a thing?

17
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,400
You couldn't help but see what I didn't want you to see.

18
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:36,500
You can say nothing is wrong, but you are still the landlord

19
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:41,800
and I am a widow with a child who rents monthly.

20
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,600
It's not just you but Hyo Seon's maternal uncle

21
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:48,400
and all the people who work in this house.

22
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:52,600
"Are you two rocks which rolled in from somewhere?" That's what those eyes say.

23
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,800
Say there ...

24
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:58,600
If I am seen like that, I don't know what they do to my daughter.

25
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:03,000
I feel so sorry for the pathetic thing, but I can't express that.

26
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,700
The feeling of beating my daughter with my hands,

27
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:10,800
you don't understand, how would you understand?

28
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,800
How would you understand that?

29
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,000
Look here, look here.

30
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Oh dear.

31
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,400
Look here, Miss Kang Seok ...

32
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,100
Is everyone here? There's no one missing?

33
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:41,800
Any person who doesn't want to work for my new wife,

34
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,000
leave right now.

35
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,600
When ypu leave, I'll give you severance pay,

36
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,200
so leave immediately.

37
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:57,300
Those who cannot treat Hyo Seon's new unni as my eldest daughter,

38
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:02,000
see me now right here.

39
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,000
Step forward.

40
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:40,800
I've packed up a hundred times in my mind.

41
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,800
First. I take out the bag.

42
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,800
I don't need the big one.

43
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:51,200
Open the bag.

44
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,400
Get the underwear.

45
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:56,400
There should be two sets.

46
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,600
Also two pairs of socks.

47
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,800
One summer outfit,

48
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:05,000
one winter outfit.

49
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:10,600
A book to read if I get bored.

50
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,700
It's done.

51
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:20,700
I almost forgot. My entire fortune of ₩227000.

52
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,800
That's all. Let's go.

53
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:30,100
A place where mom isn't. Also a place where there's no bitch Hyo Seon.

54
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:41,400
I've been searching for you for a while.

55
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:44,600
Let's go.

56
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,700
Let's go. I'm hungry.

57
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,400
What the heck are you doing?

58
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:59,000
This kid makes it awkward.

59
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,500
Sorry. I'm sorry.

60
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,700
Where are you going, kid?

61
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:10,800
You're not going home, are you?

62
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,300
You don't even know where this neighborhood is.

63
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,300
When I came here last summer,

64
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:18,100
I started at the beginning with a daytime ride.

65
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:20,400
I know anywhere and everywhere.

66
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:23,400
Even if I don't look like it, I am an expert so you can't hide from me.

67
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:38,400
Hey you! How can you leave when some one is injured?

68
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,700
I can't walk.

69
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,900
Are you okay? Wait up.

70
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:48,900
I think you're hurt.

71
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:58,200
Eun Jo! Wait for me!

72
00:06:06,300 --> 00:06:08,000
There.

73
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:17,900
Why are you walking so quickly? I'm breathless so let's go a little slower.

74
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,800
Aren't you hurting? Are you hurt somewhere?

75
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:23,800
I heard a loud sound when you fell.

76
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:27,100
It looks like something is broken. Let me see.

77
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:37,400
Look at your leg! There's blood all over and you aren't aware of it?

78
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:41,600
The bleeding isn't stopping. You're in big trouble.

79
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:44,200
Really. Don't ypu feel the pain?

80
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:48,400
I hurt! How could it not hurt? But then, what of it?

81
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,100
I hurt but what can you do about it?

82
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:04,000
I should see if there's any internal fracture so I'll take an xray first.

83
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,600
Mom.

84
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:23,270
Huh?

85
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,600
What is it, Hyo Seon?

86
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:33,800
- Who told you that? - Huh?

87
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:40,700
The kids in my class did not tease Unni.

88
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:44,800
I asked them one by one, and they all said it.

89
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:49,000
they said they didn't make fun of our family with our different last names.

90
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:55,000
And Unni, too, .... never said that.

91
00:07:57,400 --> 00:08:04,200
So, I said I am going to ask you where did you hear that said?

92
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:10,000
No, let me ask you.

93
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:28,200
I must have been mistaken.

94
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:35,000
Let's not talk about it.

95
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,600
Let's not bring it up again.

96
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,500
Yes.

97
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:47,400
Let's do that.

98
00:08:53,310 --> 00:08:59,610
If you bring it up again, I'll scold you and you will be in trouble.

99
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:20,200
Doctor. is there something wrong with her sense of pain?

100
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:24,000
Even if she is foolish, it's something I can't ever understand.

101
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:28,500
If you think there is a problem in your ability to sense pain, isn't it better if you act quickly?

102
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:35,440
At that time, what language were you singing?

103
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,800
Huh?

104
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,800
The night you were singing. You were lying on your back.

105
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:50,200
Oh. That? It's a song by a Spanish singer.

106
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:53,000
But why? Did you like it? Shall I sing it?

107
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,000
- Is Spain far away?
- Don't you know?

108
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,000
It's far. It's a 12 hour plane flight to Madrid.

109
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,200
If I flew there to hide, no one can find me.

110
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:09,600
If you go to Spain, you must also go to Barcelona. There's Gaudi, too.

111
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:12,600
Is it hard to learn Spanish?

112
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:16,900
This girl doesn't listen until a person finishes talking.

113
00:10:16,900 --> 00:10:20,400
How bizarre and interesting Gaudi's architecture is.

114
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:23,400
That's enough. Reduce the time you tutor me in math

115
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,400
and teach me Spanish.

116
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:27,000
What?

117
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,800
Please. Teach me.

118
00:10:29,800 --> 00:10:33,600
Okay? This Sunday I'm going to start,

119
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:36,400
so shorten my math class by an hour and teach me Spanish

120
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:40,800
Don't get any additional fees from Hye Seon's father. Understand?

121
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,800
Look here.

122
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:47,000
Hey you!

123
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:54,200
I don't know Spanish. What should I do?

124
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:58,400
Have they got wheels on their tongues?

125
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,600
What makes the pronunciation roll like that?

126
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:05,300
Rou, rou, rollei, rool.

127
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,500
When can I do this?

128
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,100
Oh well. I'll just work on the alphabet.

129
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,600
Spanish is not just spoken in Spain.

130
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:52,200
Because most of South American was once colonized by Spain

131
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:54,200
currently it's the most commonly spoken language there.

132
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,400
It would be very useful in the future.

133
00:12:56,400 --> 00:13:00,000
In that respect, studying Spanish as a second language—

134
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,200
-Which is the farthest?
- Huh?

135
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:04,200
Which is farther, South America or Spain?

136
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:07,600
Between them, which is farther?

137
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:10,500
Hey. You're a person who doesn't listen until the end.

138
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:14,800
Never mind. Start teaching. I'll look for a map later.

139
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:18,000
You truly are someone who doesn't listen until the end.

140
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,400
What kind of manners is that?

141
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:23,600
Further, why are you speaking informally when we are having a class?

142
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:25,400
All right. (Speaking formally)

143
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:30,200
Today, let's study the Spanish alphabet.

144
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:34,200
I studied the alphabet on my own last night, so let's move to the next lesson.

145
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:40,000
- What?
- I studied the alphabet last night so start with the send lesson.

146
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,200
Please do so. The second lesson.

147
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:06,200
The farthest place from here in South America is Ushuaia at the southern tip of Argentina.

148
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:13,900
The long narrow country in the direction of the south Pacific is Chile.

149
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
This is Argentina.

150
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,600
And this, precisely, is Ushuaia, at the end of the world.

151
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,800
As soon as I took a break from school,

152
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:29,400
I went backpacking passing through America and Mexico. When I got this far,

153
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:33,200
- I was running out of money as though a leech—
- How long did it take?

154
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,800
- You should let people finish—
- How long does it take to get there?

155
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:40,000
How much does it cost?

156
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:46,200
Are you going? Do you want to go to Ushuaia? Why do you want to go there?

157
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:49,000
Never mind. Let's study.

158
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:52,200
When the guests come it will be noisy.

159
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:54,800
There is no direct flight to Argentina.

160
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:59,000
You have to change flights in the US or Canada and fly to Buenos Aires.

161
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:04,000
You must travel two to three thousand kilometres from Buenos Aires to get to Ushuaia.

162
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:11,000
Studying today is hard.

163
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,000
Let's do it tomorrow.

164
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,500
By the way, is your knee okay?

165
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,400
Congratulations.

166
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:31,400
Yes. Yes.

167
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,200
This must be your first birthday with your new wife. Congratuations.

168
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:37,200
Thank you.

169
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:42,200
You're having to host a big party as soon as you arrived. You must be working so hard.

170
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:44,200
What hard work?

171
00:15:44,200 --> 00:15:45,600
Congratulations.

172
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:48,000
- Thank you.
- Congratulations.

173
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:22,200
Yes. This is Eun Jo's ... Hello?

174
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,700
To unlock the phone, enter the password.

175
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:37,400
Nui. It's Jeong Woo. Why aren't you answering?

176
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:42,700
Dad has gambled away all the money he got from you and Mom.

177
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:46,000
He said he was going to you and Mom. He just left.

178
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,410
I think he's going to cause a ruckus.

179
00:16:48,410 --> 00:16:52,500
My heart is pounding. I think I'm going to die.

180
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:55,600
Nui, You must do well.

181
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:02,200
Am I someone you forgot?

182
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:06,100
It doesn't matter. I won't forget. Exactly what kind of parent ...

183
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:09,900
I am your card. You are my respon-

184
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,400
siblilty.

185
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:15,000
If you want to save it, press 1. If you want ...

186
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,600
Wait. Wait.

187
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:20,000
The message won't be saved.

188
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:24,000
What did she say? What did this girl say?

189
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:38,900
I will pour you a drink.

190
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:17,300
Unni.

191
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:23,400
You didn't get a gift for Dad, did you?

192
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:28,700
I ... even did it for you.

193
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
But we will use just one card.

194
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,900
- I don't want to.
- Unni.

195
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:42,400
Then, don't use a card. Just give the present.

196
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,200
I don't want to.

197
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:47,200
Unni, then ...

198
00:18:48,510 --> 00:18:51,580
I want you to understand what I say.

199
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,400
Leave me alone.

200
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:57,040
Unni.

201
00:18:58,100 --> 00:19:00,900
Why are you so scary?

202
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,700
Unni. This ...

203
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:13,100
Your phone keeps ringing. I think you keep getting voice messages.

204
00:19:14,010 --> 00:19:16,310
Why are you touching someone else's stuff?

205
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:19,600
That's not it.

206
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:25,000
I went to our bedroom to get this and it kept vibrating on your desk.

207
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:35,500
Why are you following me?

208
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:41,100
It's boring for you to be alone.

209
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Who is it?

210
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,000
Who is it?

211
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:59,200
Where's your uncle?

212
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:02,400
Uncle? Which one?

213
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:04,800
I mean your mother's younger brother.

214
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,800
Why can't you even recall something like that?

215
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:25,800
Did you give our address to that man or not?

216
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:30,900
Well... I did not give our address to that man.

217
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:35,000
But I gave him our business card.

218
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:40,200
Why? How can you do something like that?

219
00:20:40,200 --> 00:20:42,700
Does your brain even work?

220
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:50,400
Didn't I say that I didn't tell him? But I only gave him our business card. That's all.

221
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,300
What's happened?

222
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:58,800
I just gave him our card. I don't know why the heck she was yelling at me for.

223
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:19,200
Go ahead.

224
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:22,200
- What song should I sing now?
- Just sing quickly.

225
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:24,800
Applause! Applause!

226
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:33,700
Whenever it rains, I think of that person.

227
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:41,400
The person who always remain in silence.

228
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:49,700
Who hides his love in isolation.

229
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:57,000
The person whom I cannot forget.

230
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:03,700
The person who cries alone.
- Good...

231
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:07,930
One day he asked me in the car.

232
00:22:07,930 --> 00:22:11,500
Will he think of me just once?

233
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:20,200
I really want to see that person.

234
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:26,800
I still miss that person.

235
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:34,000
Hey!

236
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:40,430
Do you know that?

237
00:22:41,390 --> 00:22:44,670
I taught her that song.

238
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:53,000
- So...
- Get up right now.

239
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:57,200
So...

240
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:32,100
I'll go outside.

241
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:35,000
Call me if you need anything.

242
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:56,000
I should just kill you.

243
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:57,200
Then kill me.

244
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:59,600
I really want to to kill you.

245
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:03,200
Kill me! Just kill me then!

246
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:05,000
Have you gone crazy?

247
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:08,500
Can I live without going crazy?

248
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:12,600
Without Kang Sook...

249
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:16,000
can I live without going crazy?

250
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,200
Go die then.

251
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:23,200
The Kang Sook you yearn for does not exist anymore.

252
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:26,000
Don't say that.

253
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:31,800
I really love your mom.

254
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:34,800
You mean the woman whom you sold?

255
00:24:34,800 --> 00:24:37,600
Don't pretend to be so high and mignty.

256
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:40,800
If I were to bring you lots of money right now,

257
00:24:40,800 --> 00:24:44,000
you would do the same thing.

258
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,200
So do you need more money?

259
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:48,600
I told you don't do that.

260
00:24:48,600 --> 00:24:53,200
I missed your mother so I came here.

261
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:57,200
I'm not here for money.

262
00:24:57,200 --> 00:25:00,800
Uncle, I'll carry it.

263
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:04,600
Uncle, let's go in. I said I'll bring it over.

264
00:25:04,600 --> 00:25:07,400
Can you even move it by yourself?

265
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:10,400
We can carry it together then.

266
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:15,200
